# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/470-fix-sdlc-execute-closing-worker-panes-while-their-background-work-runs/requirements.md
Feature: Fix sdlc-execute closing worker panes while their background work runs

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A worker waiting on its background gate keeps its pane
    Given a verify worker that writes ".nmg-sdlc/handoffs/42-verify.json.waiting" and ends its turn without a handoff
    When the background gate finishes and the worker resumes and writes a passed handoff
    Then no pane is closed before that handoff
    And the controller polled "agent wait --until working --timeout 60000"
    And the issue proceeds to deliver

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A settled worker without a handoff or marker is reminded once
    Given a stale waiting marker from an earlier invocation
    And a verify worker that ends its turn without a handoff
    When the controller reminds it and it writes a passed handoff
    Then exactly one reminder names the handoff path and the waiting marker path
    And the issue proceeds to deliver

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A lost verify handoff is retried as verify
    Given a verify worker that ends without a handoff and ignores the reminder
    When the controller selects the next step
    Then it dispatches verify again with "missing_handoff" evidence

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Process loss and blocked workers close without a reminder
    Given a verify worker reported as "<state>" without a handoff
    When the controller observes it
    Then it sends no reminder and does no resume wait
    And the next verify prompt names "<reasonCode>"

    Examples:
      | state   | reasonCode      |
      |         | process_lost    |
      | blocked | missing_handoff |

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: A branch with no commits is implemented before it is verified
    Given a branch just created by start with no commits relative to main
    When the controller selects the next step
    Then it dispatches implement, then verify, then deliver
